# Design semantics guard

**Canonical**: [`docs/DESIGN_SEMANTICS.md`](../docs/DESIGN_SEMANTICS.md) · global `npcdotcom-philosophy` when present

## IF designing / planning / specifying THEN

1. Separate **recognition (object)** from **factors (function · action · property)**
2. Propose **factor registration / combination** first — not a class tree
3. Treat GoF / inheritance / class OOP as **optional references**, never required
4. Do not equate “object” with code `class`
5. Do not treat language/stack (Rust, C++, …) as philosophy core

## Misalignment → stop

Recognition forced into inheritance · factors omitted · action equated only to “runtime” · stack elevated to core · image/terms unaligned before Do

→ Realign with DESIGN_SEMANTICS + user `>` / dialogue before `*-conduct`
